        ],
        "title": "FastAPI",
        "version": "0.1.0",
        "tagline": "Look up geolocation, network and robot-detection info for any IP address via realip.cc",
        "homepage": "https://realip.cc",
        "docs_url": "https://realip.cc/docs",
        "about_md": "[realip.cc](https://realip.cc) is a free IP geolocation and network-info service built on FastAPI and maintained by Bboysoul. The OpenAPI document is titled simply \"FastAPI\" because it inherits the framework default, but the actual product is IP lookup at `https://realip.cc`.\n\nWhat you typically get back for a given IP address:\n\n- IP address, city, province, country, continent and ISO country code\n- ISP / network owner and network range\n- Coordinates (latitude / longitude) and postal code\n- Timezone\n- Data update timestamp\n- A robot / bot classification signal and an IP rank score\n\nOperational notes: the service is open and does not document an API key requirement. Concurrent requests are rate-limited (specific thresholds are not published). CORS is reported as disabled, so calls are best made from server-side code. Human-readable docs live at `/docs` (Swagger UI). The author also publishes a blog at [bboy.app](https://www.bboy.app).",
        "entity_desc": {
          "index_get": "Root lookup that returns IP geolocation and network info for the caller (or a supplied IP) — served from `/`.",
          "iprank": "IP reputation / rank score for a given address, used to gauge how suspicious an IP is.",
          "json": "JSON-formatted IP info response variant.",
          "robot": "Robot / bot detection signal indicating whether the IP looks like an automated client.",
          "simple": "Minimal / plain-text variant of the IP lookup response.",
          "table": "Tabular (human-readable) variant of the IP lookup response."
        },
        "auth": false
      },
      "config": {
        "auth": {
          "prefix": "Bearer"
        },
        "headers": {
          "content-type": "application/json"
        },
        "docs_order": [
          "ts",
          "py",
          "php",
          "go",
          "rb",
          "lua"
        ]
      },
